A\r\n  finding is a WARN, and an ERROR under `--strict`.\r\n\r\n## Critique dispositions\r\n\r\nRound 1 (fresh Sol, 2026-11-04): CHANGES-REQUESTED, three MINORs.\r\n\r\n- **S2, adopted.** The Context's denial of gate authority is replaced by the\r\n  `## Trust` section above, which reads \"so a test file takes part in a gate\"\r\n  and consolidates the existing behaviour; no check is added.\r\n- **S5, adopted.** The delta now reads \"four values to the finding domain: a\r\n  misplaced tag, a malformed tag, an unknown TC and an unreadable file\".\r\n- **S1, adopted.** The Done-when now reads \"WI-997, the tag-migration row, is\r\n  filed on trunk before this row is claimed\", and WI-997 is filed with this\r\n  disposition, needing this row. WI-995 needs WI-997, so it lands before row\r\n  2's gate.\r\n\r\nThe S6 pre-answer's `needs` was stale beside the frontmatter and is corrected.\r\n\r\n## Scope critique, pre-answered\r\n\r\n- **S1.** There is one landable deliverable: the reader, its check and its\r\n  regressions. The text, the spine rows and the RESYNC entry are true only\r\n  once it lands, so they ride with it. The migration of this repository's\r\n  tests is split off as its own row (Migration).\r\n- **S2.** A tag can refuse a gate and can pass nothing (`## Trust`). Row 2\r\n  carries the authority to select tests.\r\n- **S3.** Closed coverage. Read positions are an enumerated set, every other\r\n  declaration under the tests root is refused (deny by default), non-docstring\r\n  string literals are excluded by construction (AST), and the four refusals\r\n  are enumerated. The bound is stated in the Coverage bound item.\r\n- **S4.** `single`: it touches two script families (`gen_arch_map`,\r\n  `check_trajectory` / `trajectory_arch`) and promises behaviour over an\r\n  input space.\r\n- **S5.** Context, \"Architectural delta\". The change is in scope, on an\r\n  existing seam.\r\n- **S6.** `needs = [\"OI-120\", \"OI-125\"]`, the ruled calls that fix the token\r\n  and the interim check. No\r\n  queued row touches these files (grep of `docs/work/queued` and\r\n  `docs/work/active`). It is stdlib only (`ast`, `tokenize`, `re`), with no\r\n  ledger row.\r\n- **S7.** No mechanism beyond the ruled reader and its refusals. Each\r\n  refusal has a reachable scenario: a misplaced comment tag or a one-line\r\n  docstring tag drops a test out of row 2's set with no word; a retired TC\r\n  leaves a dangling tag; an unparseable file would read as \"no tags\".\r\n- **B4.** No owner act and no credential in this row.\r\n[test.TC-200]\r\nverifies = [\"LLR-204\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"The grammar and the policy, separately, because they fail separately. THE GRAMMAR, driven directly on the shared function both the map column and the coverage percentage read, so a divergence between the two is unrepresentable: a declaration token opening a line yields its spine ids; prose naming ids without the token yields none; a token PRECEDED by prose yields none, including the two shapes that had previously harvested a sentence denying a link as a declaration of it; whitespace, comment markers and quote characters may precede the token and nothing else may; a wrapped list continuation line declares nothing. THE POLICY, driven through the real command line on a real bootstrapped scaffold rather than by reading the code: with a threshold declared in the policy home and a live design row that no source declaration names, the report prints the shortfall and exits ZERO, and only the explicit strict arm turns the same reading into a nonzero exit - which is what makes the threshold a gate a repository opts into rather than one the delivered package arms on its behalf.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-204 only — its delivered grammar/policy arm; SR-163's complete join and shipped-file universe are NOT covered here\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_ids_is_the_one_definition_of_a_declaration; tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_cli_is_warn_first_and_strict_only_on_demand\"\"\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\n\r\n[test.TC-201]\r\n[requirement.SR-163]\r\ntitle = \"Every shipped file maps to a stakeholder outcome\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-038\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"MAINTAINER\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"Every file the delivered package ships shall map, through the declared shipped-file inventory and its recorded exclusions, to at least one system requirement whose references resolve to a stakeholder need — generated outputs mapping through their generator — with missing files, stale inventory entries, unresolved references and unmapped files reported under the declared warning-to-gating policy.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-038 — a supplied file with no recorded purpose is inherited scope creep, and its absence of purpose must be a named coverage finding rather than hidden in the tree. SN-038 had no citing SR. The scaffold MAPPING is the natural declared inventory: it already enumerates what ships, so the coverage universe is a declaration that exists rather than a second list that drifts.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A declared inventory defines the universe and exclusions; a shipped file absent from it, a stale entry naming a file that no longer ships, an entry whose requirement reference does not resolve to a need, and a file with no mapping are each reported; the declared policy assigns warn versus gate per class; a generated output maps through its generator's row.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"M\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-001\"]\r\n\r\n\r\n[test.TC-001]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-157\", \"LLR-001\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the trace suite; a linked chain is orphan-free and an injected orphan fails --strict.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-001 (parent SR-157)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_trace.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\n\r\n[test.TC-002]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-157\", \"LLR-002\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the registry-checks suite; duplicate/malformed ids and mis-columned rows fail --strict-integrity.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-002 (parent SR-157)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_registry_checks.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\n\r\n[test.TC-003]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-157\", \"LLR-003\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the registry-checks suite; leftover -000 rows, empty/out-of-vocab fields, and (once the spine is phased) an approved row whose Phase is not a full-cell bare integer (blank, prefixed like P1/v2, or unparseable) are flagged.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-003 (parent SR-157)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_registry_checks.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\n\r\n[test.TC-004]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-157\", \"LLR-004\"]\r\nlevel = \"Unit\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the acceptance-criteria advisory suite; an unpinned comparative warns without changing the exit code.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-004 (parent SR-157)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_ac_advisory.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\n\r\n[test.TC-005]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-157\", \"LLR-005\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the off-spine registry suites; PB and current REPO/legacy MOD back-link findings fire and -000 rows are ignored.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-005 (parent SR-157)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_modules_registry.py;tests/test_procurement.py;tests/test_assets.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
